+- R-1060 — Medium, THE SECRET DETECTOR `find_forbidden_surface_tokens` READS ANY WORD ENDING IN "sk" FOLLOWED BY A HYPHEN AS AN API KEY, SO THE GUARD TEST OVER THE VIEWER PAGE FAILS ON THIS BRANCH'S OWN NAME. Raised by the planner and reviewer of F026's first session at round 3's gate, from the one failure of that round's G4, which the worker reported and did not repair. SEARCHED BEFORE MINTING (checklist item 30): `sk-` beside `false positive`, `task-` and `word boundary` in this record and its archive find no finding describing it. MEASURED at `753f44bd`: the alternative `sk-[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{8,}` of `_SECRET_RE` in `packages/orchestration/redaction_patterns.py` carries no left boundary and the whole pattern is case-insensitive, so `find_forbidden_surface_tokens` returns a finding for `feature/f026-task-edit-runtime`, for `risk-assessment-notes` and for `a desk-organizer here`; the viewer page of `tests/ui_contracts/test_graph_architecture.py` embeds the current branch name seven times, so `test_no_raw_leaks_in_viewer` fails in any checkout of this branch, which is what hosted CI checks out; the five other `sk-` patterns under `packages/` and `scripts/` require 12 or more characters or a word boundary and were not measured further. WHY MEDIUM: a guard over production output is red on legitimate text, which blocks this branch's pull request and would redact ordinary words wherever the detector is used next. FIX: the `sk-` alternative matches only at a token start — not directly after a letter or a digit — so a key after a space, an equals sign, a quote, a slash or a hyphen, or at the start of the text, is still found; a test pins both the false positives gone and those true positives kept. Owner: F026.
